{"id":"s3.1.11","slug":"function-inverses","title":"Function Inverses","content":"<p class=\"mb-4\">To find the value of an inverse function at a specific point, $f^{-1}(c)$, it's faster to solve the equation $f(y) = c$ for $y$, rather than finding the general inverse function first.</p><p class=\"mb-4\">For $f(x) = \\frac{3}{2}x - 2$, to find $f^{-1}(3)$, set $3 = \\frac{3}{2}y - 2$. Solving for $y$ gives $5 = \\frac{3}{2}y$, so $y = \\frac{10}{3}$.</p><p class=\"mb-4\">For the special case $f(x) = \\frac{ax+b}{cx+d}$, the inverse is $f^{-1}(x) = \\frac{-dx+b}{cx-a}$.</p>","summary":"To find the value of an inverse function at a specific point, , it's faster to solve the equation for , rather than finding the general inverse function first.","generation_guideline":"Generate a problem asking for the value of an inverse function at a specific point, like `f⁻¹(c)`.","questions":[{"id":1,"text":"If $f(x) = 3x + 2$, find $f^{-1}(-2)$.","answer":"-4/3","kind":"exact","tags":["functions","logs-exponents"]},{"id":2,"text":"If $f(x) = \\frac{4x}{5}$, find $f^{-1}(2)$.","answer":"2.5","kind":"exact","tags":["fractions","functions","logs-exponents"]},{"id":3,"text":"If $f(x) = 2 - 3x$, find $f^{-1}(1)$.","answer":"1/3","kind":"exact","tags":["functions","logs-exponents"]},{"id":4,"text":"If $f(x) = x^2 - 1$ and $x > 0$, find $f^{-1}(8)$.","answer":"3","kind":"exact","tags":["functions","logs-exponents"]},{"id":5,"text":"If $f(x) = 5 + 3x$, find $f^{-1}(-2)$.","answer":"-7/3","kind":"exact","tags":["functions","logs-exponents"]},{"id":6,"text":"If $f(x) = 4 - 3x$, find $f^{-1}(2)$.","answer":"2/3","kind":"exact","tags":["functions","logs-exponents"]},{"id":7,"text":"If $f(x) = \\frac{8}{3+x}$, find $f^{-1}(2)$.","answer":"1","kind":"exact","tags":["fractions","functions","logs-exponents"]},{"id":8,"text":"If $f(x) = \\frac{3-2x}{4}$, find $f^{-1}(-1)$.","answer":"3.5","kind":"exact","tags":["fractions","functions","logs-exponents"]},{"id":9,"text":"If $f(x) = \\frac{x^3}{3} + 